From e6561f146e8cf0ea90a08f74126d105849794b34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Stimola
 <1268108-francesco-stimola@users.noreply.gitlab.freedesktop.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:34:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] frontends/va: export interlaced surfaces through a
 progressive copy

nouveau decodes into interlaced surfaces, which vaExportSurfaceHandle
rejects, so Firefox falls back to software decoding.

Export a progressive NV12 copy instead, woven by the compositor on the
first export and refreshed after each decode, video processing or
vaPutImage. Write-only exports are still rejected. Drivers with
progressive buffers are not affected.

Tested-by: Kush Chandak <kushc451@gmail.com>
Generated-by: Claude Code (Claude Opus 5.5)
