From 82cd6f90587348d20efffcd059e71d93019c62bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Stimola
 <1268108-francesco-stimola@users.noreply.gitlab.freedesktop.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:21:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] nouveau: pass chroma_format_idc to the vp3 H.264
 decoder

The H.264 picture parameters for BSP and VP both have a
chroma_format_idc field, but nouveau always sets 4:2:0 (in the BSP
structure the field was still called unk00). Monochrome streams, which
the High profile allows, are then parsed as if they carried chroma, and
every picture comes out wrong, luma included.

Pass the stream's value to both engines. With 4:0:0 the decoder leaves
the chroma planes alone, and the VA frontend clears them to grey when
it allocates the surface.

Backport-to: *
Tested-by: Kush Chandak <kushc451@gmail.com>
Generated-by: Claude Code (Claude Opus 5.5)
