From 3eb3b967b6b3483dced4e29e16886f62012384cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Stimola
 <1268108-francesco-stimola@users.noreply.gitlab.freedesktop.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:21:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] nouveau: tell the vp3 H.264 decoder whether a picture
 is MBAFF

BSP and VP take mb_adaptive_frame_field_flag from the SPS, but MBAFF
only applies to frame pictures: the field pictures of a stream that
enables it are not MBAFF coded. The decoder reads them as if they were,
so streams that mix field pictures and MBAFF frames, as interlaced
broadcasts do, decode into blocks and garbage.

Pass MbaffFrameFlag instead: the SPS flag for frames, 0 for fields.

